<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kamakura</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kamakura is a coastal city south of Tokyo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanagawa-prefecture">Kanagawa Prefecture</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoritomo">Minamoto no Yoritomo</a> made it the seat of his warrior government in the 1180s, and it remained the capital of the Kamakura <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a> until 1333, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nitta-yoshisada">Nitta Yoshisada</a> stormed it. It then became the seat of the Ashikaga governors of the Kanto. Its Great Buddha and Zen temples are famous.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kamakura.jpg" alt="Kamakura" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Urashimataro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaguraden-Hachimangu_Kamakura.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
